 # Full Cloud Density Function
 
-Also called: Procedural Cloud Density Function
 
 ## Overview
-The Full Cloud Density Function is a procedural method for computing volumetric cloud density by combining a vertical atmospheric profile with horizontal noise-based structures and a global coverage mask [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Procedural 3D Worley-Perlin Fractal Noise Density](5267-procedural-3d-worley-perlin-fractal-noise.md) by explicitly separating vertical stratification from horizontal structural modulation [S1, unofficial].
+The Full Cloud Density Function is a procedural method for computing volumetric cloud density by combining a vertical atmospheric profile with horizontal noise-based structures and a global coverage mask [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Procedural 3D Worley-Perlin Fractal Noise Density](5267-procedural-3d-worley-perlin-fractal-noise-density.md) by explicitly separating vertical stratification from horizontal structural modulation [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `point`: A 3D vector representing the sample position in world space.
-- `lod`: Level of detail parameter for high-frequency noise.
-- `radius`: Radius of the cloud volume.
-- `cloud_scale`: Scaling factor for low-frequency cloud shapes.
-- `detail_scale`: Scaling factor for high-frequency noise detail.
-- `gradient`, `multiplier`, `threshold`, `cap`: Tuning parameters for density modulation [S1, unofficial].
-- `powder_decay`: Parameter for the powder sugar scattering effect [S1, unofficial].
